# Data Preparation

This directory contains the three notebooks that form the data preparation pipeline. They run in sequence as tasks within the `data-preprocessing-job` (see [`resources/data-preparation-resource.yml`](../resources/data-preparation-resource.yml), task keys `RawDataIngest` → `PreprocessRawData` → `VectorSearchIndex`).

## Notebooks

| Notebook | Task key | What it does |
|----------|----------|--------------|
| `DataIngestion.py` | `RawDataIngest` | Fetches an XML sitemap from `data_source_url`, scrapes each page with BeautifulSoup in parallel via a Spark pandas UDF, and writes raw text to a Unity Catalog Delta table. |
| `DataPreprocessing.py` | `PreprocessRawData` | Reads the raw table, splits documents into chunks using a HuggingFace tokenizer and LangChain text splitter, and writes the preprocessed table used for indexing. |
| `VectorSearch.py` | `VectorSearchIndex` | Creates or syncs a Databricks Vector Search index over the preprocessed table using the `databricks-gte-large-en` embedding model. |

All three notebooks install dependencies from `../requirements.txt` at the bundle root.

## Running manually

Each notebook accepts Databricks widget parameters (`uc_catalog`, `schema`, `raw_data_table`, etc.) that are also passed as `base_parameters` in the job definition. You can run any notebook interactively in your dev workspace by attaching it to a cluster and setting the widget values.

## Customizing

To use your own data source, modify `DataIngestion.py`:
- Change the `data_source_url` widget default to your sitemap or API endpoint.
- Adapt the HTML parsing logic in the `fetch_and_parse` function for your document structure.

For deployment and job setup, see [`resources/README_agentops.md`](../resources/README_agentops.md).
